#%RAML 1.0 SecurityScheme
type: OAuth 2.0
description: |
  Machine-to-machine only. There is no authorization-code flow: every consumer
  of this platform is a system, and end-user identity is carried in the calling
  application's own session instead of in this token.

  In a deployed environment the token is issued by Anypoint Access Management or
  the enterprise IdP and validated by an API Manager JWT policy. No Mule
  application ever issues a token.
describedBy:
  headers:
    Authorization:
      type: string
      example: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJSUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...
  responses:
    401:
      description: Missing, expired or invalid token.
    403:
      description: Valid token without the required scope.
settings:
  accessTokenUri: https://auth.acme-retail.example.com/oauth/token
  authorizationGrants: [client_credentials]
  scopes:
    - customer:read
    - insights:read
    - ai:invoke
    - pii:read
